INT. RECORDING BOOTH, DEFUNCT RADIO STATION - NIGHT

Egg-crate foam on every wall. A dusty microphone on a boom. A reel-to-reel recorder with one reel running. A lamp with a green glass shade.

MIRIAM OKONKWO-DELACROIX (60s, hair gone white, wool coat still buttoned) sits at the console with a thermos and a cassette recorder. A red light glows on the cassette.

MIRIAM
(into microphone)
Testing. One, two. This is Miriam, speaking into the old microphone, Tuesday the ninth.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel, younger, bright)
Good evening and welcome to the Night Owl Hour. I'm Miriam Okonkwo, keeping you company until dawn.

MIRIAM
That voice has no idea.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
Tonight's request comes from a gentleman in Marlow Street, who writes: play something for my wife, we've been married thirty years.

MIRIAM
Thirty years. I remember that card.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
And so, for Walter and Eleanor. Here's the Platters.

MIRIAM
Walter died in the spring. Eleanor wrote to tell me.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
This one is for the ones who stay up late.

MIRIAM
I'm staying up. Don't worry.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
Which is most of us, if we're honest.

MIRIAM
Most of us. That's right.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
Because the night is long, and the dial is lonely, and I'm here.

MIRIAM
I am here. I'm here, dear.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel, a fade)
Stay tuned. I'll be back after this song.

MIRIAM
(into microphone)
Station's closing Friday. Last transmission is at midnight. I thought I'd record a goodbye. For whoever's listening.

MIRIAM (V.O.)
(from the reel)
Good night, owls.

MIRIAM
(into microphone)
Good night, owls.
